    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Choose a sensible mass unit for each.\n(a) A rubber eraser\n(b) A school bag\n(c) A loaded cement truck",
        "solution_text": "(a) An eraser is light. Use grams ($\\text{g}$).\n(b) A school bag has a mass of a few kilograms. Use kilograms ($\\text{kg}$).\n(c) A loaded truck is very heavy, with a mass of thousands of kilograms. Use tonnes ($\\text{t}$)."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Choose between scales that read to the nearest $10\\text{ g}$ and precision scales to measure a $3\\text{ g}$ seed sample.\n(b) A crate has a mass of about $31\\text{ kg}$. Choose between bench scales with a maximum capacity of $8\\text{ kg}$ and platform scales with a maximum capacity of $120\\text{ kg}$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Use precision scales reading grams. A reading to the nearest $10\\text{ g}$ is too coarse for a $3\\text{ g}$ sample.\n(b) $31\\text{ kg}>8\\text{ kg}$, so the crate is too heavy for the bench scales.\n$31\\text{ kg}<120\\text{ kg}$, so use the platform scales reading kilograms."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) A guitar label gives its mass as $5.8\\text{ g}$. Correct the likely unit error.\n(b) Can scales with a maximum capacity of $40\\text{ kg}$ measure a box expected to have a mass of $87\\text{ kg}$? Explain.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $5.8\\text{ g}$ is far too light for a guitar. The sensible mass is $5.8\\text{ kg}$.\n(b) $87\\text{ kg}>40\\text{ kg}$. No; the box exceeds the scales' maximum capacity. Use a higher-capacity device."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Choose a sensible mass unit and measuring device for each.\n(a) $250$ grams of rice for a recipe\n(b) A person's mass\n(c) A loaded gravel truck",
        "solution_text": "(a) Use grams ($\\text{g}$) and kitchen scales. Kitchen scales measure small ingredient masses.\n(b) Use kilograms ($\\text{kg}$) and bathroom scales with enough capacity for the person.\n(c) Use tonnes ($\\text{t}$) and a weighbridge. A loaded truck has a mass of thousands of kilograms and needs a device designed for heavy vehicles."
      }
    ],
